NAME
     netstat - sockets, and what they are doing

SYNOPSIS
     netstat [-a] [-n] [-t] [-u] [-l] [-p]
     ss [-a] [-n] [-t] [-u] [-l] [-p]

DESCRIPTION
     netstat prints the sockets: protocol, how much is queued each way,
     the two addresses, the state, and with -p the process.

OPTIONS
     -a   all sockets, not only the connected ones
     -n   numbers rather than names
     -t   TCP only
     -u   UDP only
     -l   only the ones listening
     -p   the process that has it

SEE ALSO
     lsof(1), ip(8), tcpdump(1), /proc/net/tcp
